  "criticalFindings": [
    "A01 ↔ A-FU01 and D02 ↔ D-FU01 are near-identical decision structures; rewording is not additional information by itself.",
    "D-FU02 and D-FU03 are opposite-worded versions of the same D06 scenario, not independent item-information.",
    "C-FU01/C-FU05 repeat C01/C05; B-FU01/B-FU03/B-FU05 share a conflict template but may add meaning when different social contexts truly matter.",
    "Follow-up item bank itself has redundancy clusters (e.g. A-FU01/02/06/07, B-FU01/03/05, C-FU01/05/07, D-FU01/02/03/05/06, E-FU01/02/03).",
    "A02 and D03 already have strong cross-axis overlap (new vs familiar places); adding more similar items could amplify, not fix, non-independence.",
    "Original B02 asks sociability/lone leisure but B-FU09 tests inability to choose between values, so its former old-item overlap metadata was conceptually misleading.",
    "No extra questionnaire format yet has calibrated discrimination or a psychometric score conversion; NO auto-classification from Y/N."
  ],
